<%# locals: (group:, count:) %>
<%# WHY: the gig card's footer row, in the kicker's type so the kicker that opens the card has a twin closing it; the hairline and the 44px row, the WCAG 2.5.5 target, part it from what sits above, which the `card-break` margin also clears. `relative z-1` lifts it over the hero's stretched name link, and the empty gig slot draws the same row. The link names Upcoming because a bare events URL opens Active for whoever runs the events, and this row promises upcoming gigs to every member. %>
<%= link_to group_events_path(group, scope: "upcoming", category: [ "gig" ]), class: "group relative z-1 mt-[calc(var(--spacing-card-break)-var(--spacing-card-row))] flex min-h-11 items-center justify-between border-t border-base-content/10 pt-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider" do %>
  <span class="group-hover:underline">All upcoming gigs (<%= count_label(count) %>)</span><%= icon :go_to, class: "size-icon-inline" %>
<% end %>
